<HR><BR>
<P></tt><B><FONT COLOR="#000000"><FONT SIZE=+3>Level Costs (Cash)</FONT></FONT></B><BR><tt>


Formula seems to be:

cashcost = (guildlvl)*(guildlvl)*(15)

Which is to say, take your guild lvl, square it, and multiply by 15.  
So if you are at a guild lvl of 5, the cost is 5*5*15 = 375 gold.  
For guild lvl of 60, it is 60*60*15 = 54000 gold.

Gol's cumulative guild cost calculator is:

2.5n(n+1)(2n+1)

Where n=(characterlevel-15), and cumulative cost is the total cost 
from 0 to n.  Don't forget to subtract the costs of joining levels 
which are free, and don't forget to place joining levels as high as 
possible, in other words, join guilds so that you join those with most 
levels first and least level last.




